From 55872c89ea07992fbd2ab2e72abdce5711679c2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Etienne Carriere <etienne.carriere@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 19 Dec 2023 09:27:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 0286/1695] plat-stm32mp1: SiP SMC service for PWR access

Implement a SiP SMC based interface fir the non-secure world to
access PWR registers and non-secure regulators. The service is
embedded upon CFG_STM32_PWR_SIP=y.

PWR registers and their bit fields that non-secure is allowed to access
using SiP SMC service may depend on the resources registered at build
time or initialization time in OP-TEE core.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 4c2d4136f11f4431f0b684f00c93289e9c89ec1f plat-stm32mp1: SiP SMC service for PWR access]
Change-Id: Icc180bdaab00536a4996e1329d92e16b2d543f2f
Signed-off-by: Etienne Carriere <etienne.carriere@st.com>
